            <ArticleTitle>[Coronary artery of the heart reconstructions after endarterectomy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>17-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary endarterectomy is necessary in up to 37% of patients undergoing coronary artery bypass grafting surgery. Bypass grafting of &quot;inoperable arteries&quot; allows complete revascularization, improves prognosis and quality of life of patients with diffusely diseased coronary arteries. The article considers reconstructive techniques for coronary arteries after endarterectomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
